@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+# Stock correctness implementation plan
+
+1. Add a reusable HTTP 409 conflict exception/handler and use it for inventory conflicts and forbidden post-cancellation status transitions.
+2. Centralize effective product stock lookup and proposed-cart validation in the shop cart facade. Validate requested positive quantities against the product’s stock before adding, replacing, or batch-mutating any line. Build/validate the complete batch proposal first, then apply it, so batch operations are atomic; preserve zero/removal/decrease behaviour.
+3. Fix checkout inventory handling in the core order service: validate every cart line by SKU and quantity before order creation/payment side effects, then decrement exactly the matched product’s inventory in the same transaction. Remove the bad order-line-id lookup and mismatch logging/continue behaviour.
+4. Make both checkout APIs preserve and expose stock conflicts as HTTP 409 instead of converting them to 503/400 responses.
+5. Add idempotent cancellation restoration and terminal cancellation rules to order status updates. Restore each order line by SKU only on the transition into `CANCELED`; reject every later non-canceled transition with 409 and leave stock unchanged.
+6. Make the v2 readable product response explicitly derive `available` and `canBePurchased` from merchant availability plus positive stock, including restocking and merchant-forced-unavailable cases.
+7. Add focused unit/integration coverage where the existing test setup permits, then run the Maven build and relevant tests; document any environment/test limitations.
